From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 056/147] hjviewer: ui: remote-session: the session toolbar and
 the phone overlays in the new look

The screens of a remote session still had RustDesk's solid blue tiles and bars. Now, in
the palette, radii and text of hjv_style.dart (visuals only; sizes that the toolbar's
drag and the canvas depend on are kept):

- Desktop toolbar: the bar is a floating card (card colour, thin border, soft shadow),
  rounded on the side facing away from its docked edge like the handle. Buttons are
  icons in the secondary text colour with the hover colour under them; pinned, the
  current display, an open menu and a call going on are primarySoft/primary; close,
  a call being set up and recording use the danger colour. The monitor layout and
  the display switchers follow the palette.
- Toolbar menus: radius 12 with inset 28 px rows, the hover colour on rows, the
  palette's text, icon and divider colours, the app's popup menu shadow.
- Handle: a small card with the secondary text colour icons, a shadow when alone.
- Remote window tabs: the selected tab's line in the palette's primary; the
  relative mouse mode hint as a soft warning chip.
- Phone: the bottom bar is a card with a hairline on top and outlined icons, close
  in the danger colour; the key bar shows keycaps (on: primarySoft/primary, kept
  on: primary); the gesture help has a segmented control and calm pictograms; the
  display options use the theme's dividers and display chips; the FAB uses the
  palette's primary.

After an independent review (screens in light and dark, the diff, the code rules):

- Phone key bar: 8 px side gutters, so the keycaps no longer touch the screen
  edge; the frame colour at 85 % opacity, so the remote screen shows through
  the bar again as under upstream's dark bar (the canvas moves out of its way
  only while the soft keyboard is up).
- Gesture help: the outlined mouse and touch icons, like the bar's buttons.
- The FAB's colours and the toolbar menus' shadow come from the theme
  (the shared commit); the local overrides that repeated it are gone.
- Toolbar: the bar's card is its own builder (_hjvToolbarCard) in place of
  upstream's Material; upstream's scroll view, theme, borderWrapper and Flex
  lines stay as they were.
- Toolbar buttons: recording and a call being set up darken under the pointer
  like the other buttons that are on. The open-menu tint and its post-frame
  setState are gone.
- Voice call menu: End call in the danger colour.
- Remote tabs: selectedBorderColor back to upstream's (the pill tabs do not
  read it); the relative mouse hint's text in the text colour (it was 3.1:1
  in the light theme).

